# Documentation Rules

Every component needs three layers of documentation:

1. **JSDoc on the component** — for IDE hover hints and the MCP `get_component` response
2. **`<ComponentName>.examples.tsx`** — code examples + do's/don'ts
3. **Docs page** under `app/(docs)/components/[slug]/page.tsx`

## JSDoc standard

```tsx
/**
 * Brief one-line description of what the component does.
 *
 * More detailed description if needed — when to use it, when not to,
 * what problem it solves.
 *
 * @example Primary action
 * <Button variant="primary">Submit</Button>
 *
 * @example Destructive action
 * <Button variant="destructive">Delete</Button>
 *
 * @see Related: TextField, IconButton
 */
export const Button = (...) => { /* ... */ };
```

## Examples file format

```tsx
// src/components/Button/Button.examples.tsx
import { ButtonExamplesData } from '@/src/types/docs';

export const data: ButtonExamplesData = {
  // Concise one-liner shown on cards / search results
  tagline: 'Primary action component for all clickable actions.',

  // Code examples — render in docs + serve via MCP
  examples: [
    {
      title: 'Primary button',
      description: 'The main CTA on a page',
      code: `<Button variant="primary" size="md">Submit</Button>`,
    },
    {
      title: 'Destructive button',
      description: 'For delete or destructive actions',
      code: `<Button variant="destructive">Delete account</Button>`,
    },
    {
      title: 'Loading state',
      code: `<Button loading>Processing...</Button>`,
    },
  ],

  // Do's — what TO do
  dos: [
    'Use `primary` for the main CTA on a page (one per section)',
    'Use `destructive` for irreversible actions (delete, remove)',
    'Use `outline` or `ghost` for secondary actions',
  ],

  // Don'ts — what NOT to do
  donts: [
    'Don\'t use multiple `primary` buttons in the same section',
    'Don\'t use `destructive` for cancel/dismiss actions',
    'Don\'t hardcode button colors — use the variant prop',
  ],

  // Related components
  relatedComponents: ['IconButton', 'ButtonGroup'],
};
```

## What docs pages do not carry

Two things are deliberately absent from every component page, and from the
`data` object that feeds it. Do not add them back.

- **No accessibility section.** These components ship into internal
  dashboards, so accessibility is not a documented concern here. There is
  no `accessibility` field on `ComponentExamplesData`, no `## Accessibility`
  heading in a component's JSDoc, and no contrast/WCAG measurements in
  `dos`, `donts`, or prop descriptions. MUI's own ARIA behaviour is left
  untouched in the components — it just isn't documented.
- **No links to internal notes.** `DESIGNER_QUESTIONS.md` is an internal
  log. Never reference it — by name or by number — anywhere a reader or a
  package consumer can see it: docs pages, `*.examples.tsx` `data` fields,
  or the JSDoc on an exported symbol (that one ships in `dist/index.d.ts`).
  Record the open question in `DESIGNER_QUESTIONS.md` itself and, if the
  page needs to explain a deviation, state the deviation on its own terms.

## Writing do's and don'ts

Good do's/don'ts are **specific and actionable**:

```
✅ Good: "Use `primary` for the main CTA on a page (one per section)"
❌ Bad: "Use buttons correctly"

✅ Good: "Don't use placeholder as a replacement for label"
❌ Bad: "Don't misuse the input"
```

Frame don'ts as **what not to do**, not as warnings:

```
✅ "Don't create custom button components — extend this one"
❌ "Warning: custom buttons may cause inconsistency"
```

## Code examples — style guide

- **Self-contained.** Each example should run on its own (no missing imports or undefined state).
- **Realistic.** Use real labels like "Submit", "Delete account", "Send invite" — not "Click me" or "Button".
- **Show props.** Examples should demonstrate the prop being explained.
- **No unused props.** Don't add `size="md"` if it's the default.

```tsx
// ✅ Good — shows the variant prop
<Button variant="destructive">Delete account</Button>

// ❌ Bad — generic text and unnecessary props
<Button variant="primary" size="md" disabled={false}>Click me</Button>
```

## Docs pages

Each component has a page at `app/(docs)/components/[slug]/page.tsx` that imports from the examples file:

```tsx
// app/(docs)/components/button/page.tsx
import { data } from '@/src/components/Button/Button.examples';
import { ComponentDocsLayout } from '@/app/_components/ComponentDocsLayout';

export default function ButtonDocsPage() {
  return <ComponentDocsLayout componentName="Button" {...data} />;
}
```

The `ComponentDocsLayout` is shared and handles:
- Component preview (live rendered)
- Props table (auto-generated from TypeScript)
- Code examples with copy button
- Do's and don'ts
- Related components

## Pattern documentation

Patterns (in `src/patterns/`) are documented as full code files, not example snippets:

```tsx
// src/patterns/dashboard/dashboard.tsx
/**
 * Dashboard pattern — Standard Neoflo dashboard layout.
 *
 * Top action bar + 3-column metric cards + data table below.
 * Responsive: collapses to 1-column on mobile.
 *
 * @pattern dashboard
 */
export function DashboardPattern() {
  return (
    <Box sx={{ p: 4 }}>
      {/* ... full layout ... */}
    </Box>
  );
}
```

The MCP `get_pattern` tool returns this full code.
